    "z_score_lambda2": -3.422,
    "z_score_ap_fraction": -1.448,
    "z_score_gcc_after_top5_removal": -79.225,
    "interpretation_note": "The configuration model rewires edges randomly while preserving the degree sequence. It contains NO spatial constraint: it will freely connect Lubbock to Houston. Any geographically embedded network will therefore look 'fragile' versus this null, because the null cannot exhibit the long-range weak coupling that makes real grids hard to route across. Our large negative z-scores (e.g. z = -79 on hub-removal) quantify ERCOT's spatial embedding cost, NOT an unusual pathology. They should be read as 'ERCOT is geographic' rather than 'ERCOT is broken.'"
  },
